# Read project guidance before planning or scanning

When you are **planning a new feature**, **planning a change**, or **finding where to implement** work under `gdtracker/` or `gdtracker-api/`:

## Do this first (same project root you will edit)

1. Open that app’s **project summary / guidance**—typically **`docs/README.md`** (index), then **`docs/OVERVIEW.md`** and **`docs/FEATURES.md`** (or **`PROJECT.md`** if that is the only map).
2. Use the **feature map** and **directory map** to narrow **which routes, screens, controllers, services, or packages** own the behavior.
3. Only then run **targeted** search or open specific files those docs name.

## Why

- The docs give a **short orientation** so you do not have to read or search the whole repo to pick a starting point.
- **Workspace-wide** guidance also applies: see **project-guidance-docs** for maintenance expectations (keep docs truthful when behavior changes).

## Avoid

- Starting with repo-wide semantic search or random file walks when the **feature map** already points to the right area.
